gate: sdd.frame
skip_when: an idea, prd, rnd, or research covering the topic exists in .archcore/
budget: 3
taxonomy: Functional Scope & Behavior, Constraints & Tradeoffs
produces: idea draft
next: end

gate: sdd.require
skip_when: a prd covering the topic exists in .archcore/; or the request is feature-scoped and an idea, rnd, research, or adr covering the topic already records the problem and the goals
budget: 5
taxonomy: Functional Scope & Behavior, Interaction & UX Flow, Non-Functional Quality Attributes, Completion Signals
produces: prd; additionally journey under the illustrate condition of skills/_shared/delta-routing.md, composed per skills/_shared/journey-contract.md; journey only in callable mode from document journey draft
next: end

gate: sdd.design
skip_when: a spec covering the capability this invocation designs exists in .archcore/, or no consumer relies on the planned behavior as a contract, per the routing gate in skills/_shared/spec-contract.md
budget: 3
taxonomy: Domain & Data Model, Integration & External Dependencies, Edge Cases & Failure Handling, Constraints & Tradeoffs
produces: spec draft
next: end

gate: sdd.illustrate
skip_when: a scenario that depends_on the designed spec exists in .archcore/, or the capability does not meet the illustrate condition of skills/_shared/delta-routing.md, or skills/_shared/actor-subject-compatibility.md did not return yes
budget: 2
taxonomy: Interaction & UX Flow, Edge Cases & Failure Handling
produces: scenario draft
next: end

gate: sdd.decompose
skip_when: a plan covering the topic exists in .archcore/
budget: 0
taxonomy: none
produces: plan draft
next: end

gate: sdd.runbook
skip_when: the declared Δ introduces no operational procedure, or a guide covering the procedure exists in .archcore/
budget: 1
taxonomy: Edge Cases & Failure Handling, Completion Signals
produces: guide draft
next: end

